WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/LiveStatusPill.tsx — a PURE presentational connection-state badge
  mounted beside the Refresh control on /system-status, reflecting the useStatusLiveSSE pump:
    <span role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Live status stream: {label}, updated {rel}"
          data-status-live-state={state} class="… rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium ring-1 tabular-nums {tone.cls}">
      <dot bg-{tone}  (+animate-pulse when reconnecting)> <Icon> <label> <·> <relative>
  TONE: live → green Activity (no pulse) · reconnecting → amber Wifi (pulse) · offline → zinc WifiOff (no pulse).
  relative(now,lastUpdateAt): null → "—" · secs=max(0,floor((now-lastUpdateAt)/1000)) ·
    <5 → "just now" · <60 → "{secs}s ago" · <3600 → "{floor/60}m ago" · else "{floor/3600}h ago".
  No data hooks. The prompt itself records "Data sources: (none — pure presentational component)"; the surface's
  ONLY branches are the three connection tones + the null-timestamp relative branch — all reproduced, none hidden.

